WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.740
Canada's main index just entered correction territory after a 10% drop from its August peak. This is Modern Investing Techniques, episode 238. Next is defensive stock selection in a correction, a simulated Fortis weekly hold, then tools and techniques. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor, and this isn't financial advice.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:32.280
Always do your own research before putting real money to work.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:39.820
Friday's close in New York left the S&amp;P 500 at 6,910, down 3.7%.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:49.460
The NASDAQ composite finished at 22,618, down 5.3% on the session, down 2.66% year-to-date,

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:55.400
and up 1.09% since the practice portfolio opened on March 16th, 2026.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:05.080
The TSX composite closed Friday at 33,190, down 2.5%, and it is down 8.8% since November

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.860
11 after seven consecutive losing sessions.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:13.000
Friday alone knocked 838.88 points off that Canadian benchmark.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:19.440
U.S. markets also posted sharp losses the day after Anthropics public debut, with the

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:27.240
following 949.73 points and the NASDAQ dropping 1261.47 points.

00:01:27.923 --> 00:01:33.223
Fortis, according to Motley Fool Canada, is trading near $85 Canadian dollars as a low

00:01:33.223 --> 00:01:37.763
beta utility whose capital plan is built to support high single-digit earnings growth

00:01:38.063 --> 00:01:40.083
and mid-single-digit dividend growth.

00:01:40.523 --> 00:01:45.243
The company just delivered a quarterly earnings beat and a dividend increase, yet its price

00:01:45.243 --> 00:01:50.383
to earnings multiple sits above 24 times, which is on the higher side of its own historical

00:01:50.383 --> 00:01:50.823
range.

00:01:51.303 --> 00:01:56.003
You see a utility sitting rich versus its own history, while the index is already in

00:01:56.003 --> 00:01:56.423
a correction.

00:01:57.143 --> 00:02:00.763
Do you wait for a cheaper multiple, or do you take the lower beta shelter now?

00:02:01.343 --> 00:02:02.523
Here's how I'd think about it.

00:02:03.023 --> 00:02:06.423
Defensive stock selection in a correction is a screen, not a vibe.

00:02:06.923 --> 00:02:14.803
Five-year beta under 0.8, pay out under 70%, then dividend coverage above 1.5 times, because

00:02:14.803 --> 00:02:19.303
those names typically lose less than the market around them. Think of it like taking the

00:02:19.303 --> 00:02:24.583
heavy sedan down a gravel descent instead of the sports car. You will not set a time, but

00:02:24.583 --> 00:02:29.343
you are less likely to bounce off the road when the surface breaks up. Run that filter on

00:02:29.343 --> 00:02:34.803
TSX Utilities or consumer staples in your broker's screener. Then stack the current payout

00:02:34.803 --> 00:02:39.243
against the sector median so you are not buying a yield that the cash flow cannot support.

00:02:39.243 --> 00:02:45.383
board. After the screen, size it. Calculate how many shares a fixed $7,000 Canadian dollars

00:02:45.383 --> 00:02:50.043
would buy at the current print. And check that the position still fits your allocation rules

00:02:50.043 --> 00:02:56.183
before you place it inside a tax-free savings account, or TFSA, or a registered retirement

00:02:56.183 --> 00:03:02.723
savings plan, or RRSP. The same approach worked in the 2022 rate hike stretch, when lower

00:03:02.723 --> 00:03:08.903
beta utilities outperformed the TSX by approximately 8 percentage points on average. It fails when

00:03:08.903 --> 00:03:13.963
interest rates rise faster than expected, and compress valuations across the whole defensive

00:03:13.963 --> 00:03:19.343
group at once. Which is why a rich multiple is not a hall pass, even when beta looks calm.

00:03:20.063 --> 00:03:24.443
Grid modernization spending on both sides of the border still gives a visible multi-year

00:03:24.443 --> 00:03:29.743
capital expenditure runway that can support the earnings growth forecast even if broader growth

00:03:29.743 --> 00:03:37.384
slows. Remember, low beta is a shock absorber, not a valuation hall pass. Mondays open is the entry

00:03:37.384 --> 00:03:43.764
for a simulated weekly hold in Fortis, ticker FTS on the TSX, judged against the NASDAQ

00:03:43.764 --> 00:03:46.004
over five sessions under the published rules.

00:03:46.524 --> 00:03:52.504
This is a simulated trade for learning purposes, a $1,000 share position that demonstrates defensive

00:03:52.504 --> 00:03:58.304
stock selection, with an 8% stop loss that caps the notional loss at $80 Canadian dollars

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:59.984
if that stop is hit intraday.

00:04:00.484 --> 00:04:05.564
The catalyst is demand for lower beta names during the TSX correction, and the setup

00:04:05.564 --> 00:04:09.624
is a price near all-time highs that still clears the beta and coverage screen.

00:04:10.628 --> 00:04:15.428
After the lithium producer we close Friday, the standing constraint is to require sector

00:04:15.428 --> 00:04:20.188
rotation confirmation before entering any dividend name already showing relative weakness.

00:04:20.888 --> 00:04:22.788
Fortis is the other side of that constraint.

00:04:23.388 --> 00:04:27.808
The rotation being tested is into utilities, not out of a weak commodity group.

00:04:28.288 --> 00:04:33.588
I've cut a utility too early in a prior drawdown because I treated a 2% red day like a thesis

00:04:33.588 --> 00:04:38.808
break, which is exactly why the stop is named and dollars before the hold starts, and

00:04:38.808 --> 00:04:43.428
why the exit is the fifth close or that stop, with no discretionary override.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:48.010
The thesis is wrong before a single simulated dollar is at risk.

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:52.790
If the next earnings release shows adjusted earnings below the prior year level for that

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:59.310
quarter, the target is plus 2% to plus 5% over 5 sessions if defensive rotation continues.

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:06.370
Confidence is medium, sector rotation into defensives and a stable payout are aligned, but volume

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:11.790
has not confirmed, so this is two factors and one gap, not a high confidence stack.

00:05:12.801 --> 00:05:17.721
One correction on the book first, the MP Practice Pick logged earlier this month was

00:05:17.721 --> 00:05:23.381
voided as a tracking error, not a market outcome, so no simulated result is claimed for it

00:05:23.381 --> 00:05:25.481
and it is excluded from the running totals.

00:05:25.481 --> 00:05:31.841
Alba Marl, ticker ALB, was the last weekly hold, and earnings preview entry on a lithium

00:05:31.841 --> 00:05:37.241
producer facing lower prices but showing cost discipline, simulated from the Sunday open

00:05:37.241 --> 00:05:39.601
through Friday's close across 20 sessions.

00:05:40.081 --> 00:05:52.521
We simulated buying ALB at $93.67, and exiting at $79.70, a loss of 9.63%, or $902.00 on

00:05:52.521 --> 00:05:53.901
the $1,000 position.

00:05:53.901 --> 00:06:02.721
The NASDAQ over the same sessions fell 13.10%, so the matched window alpha was plus 3.47%,

00:06:02.721 --> 00:06:04.361
even though the trade lost money.

00:06:04.901 --> 00:06:06.301
Stated confidence was low.

00:06:06.781 --> 00:06:12.021
The invalidation, third quarter revenue or EBITDA guidance below the then current consensus

00:06:12.021 --> 00:06:17.661
range on the November 4th release never mattered, and the 8% stop was not reached.

00:06:18.161 --> 00:06:22.361
This didn't work in dollar terms, and the low confidence grade fit mixed conditions.

00:06:22.361 --> 00:06:27.261
The stop held, yet the name still lagged on a relative basis inside its own

00:06:27.261 --> 00:06:30.961
sector, because rotation pressure was not screened before entry.

00:06:31.601 --> 00:06:36.301
Sector rotation confirmation is now required before entering any dividend name already

00:06:36.301 --> 00:06:42.166
showing relative weakness. Trader, according to X, has two times single stock exchange

00:06:42.166 --> 00:06:49.786
traded funds, or ETFs, on Anthropic. ANTT for two times long, ANTZ for two times short,

00:06:49.786 --> 00:06:54.286
So a tactical view can be expressed without borrowing shares or using margin.

00:06:54.746 --> 00:07:00.846
They reset daily, so they suit only tactical trades inside a margin account or a non-registered portfolio.

00:07:01.426 --> 00:07:07.006
And they become available through any broker that supports US-listed ETFs once trading begins Monday.

00:07:07.526 --> 00:07:11.046
The structure is built for short-term trading rather than buy and hold,

00:07:11.346 --> 00:07:18.066
and the prospectus warns that holding longer than one day can diverge substantially from the stated leverage because of compounding.

00:07:18.066 --> 00:07:21.986
In a correction week, those products do the opposite of the beta screen.

00:07:22.466 --> 00:07:25.826
They amplify a one-day view instead of absorbing a drawdown.

00:07:26.406 --> 00:07:29.746
I have no financial relationship with Trader or OptionsPlay.

00:07:30.931 --> 00:07:35.931
OptionsPlay's put vertical spread scanner flags defined risk put spreads as a lower capital

00:07:35.931 --> 00:07:42.231
alternative to cash-secured puts, aimed at the 30-45-day window where Theta Decay is favorable.

00:07:42.751 --> 00:07:48.011
It shows the exact strike width and credit received so you can compare risk-defined income against

00:07:48.011 --> 00:07:53.071
naked shortputs, and it sits inside the options play platform for subscribers who already

00:07:53.071 --> 00:07:54.591
use its options flow data.

00:07:55.091 --> 00:08:00.431
A vertical spread caps both maximum gain and maximum loss at known dollar amounts before

00:08:00.431 --> 00:08:05.031
the trade is placed, which removes the open-ended risk of an un- hedged shortput.

00:08:05.491 --> 00:08:10.591
That cap is the options analog of naming the 8% stop before a sharehold is opened.

00:08:11.311 --> 00:08:15.491
Subscribers who already pull options flow from that platform can run the scanner without

00:08:15.491 --> 00:08:16.091
leaving it.

00:08:16.091 --> 00:08:22.313
Cathy Wood's firm purchased 705,982 shares of newly public and

00:08:22.313 --> 00:08:26.173
thropic on the first trading day while the broader market posted sharp

00:08:26.173 --> 00:08:30.073
losses. That ticket shows institutional interest through a volatile

00:08:30.073 --> 00:08:35.913
debut and pairing any new single stock ETF with a small ARKK sleeve would be

00:08:35.913 --> 00:08:39.773
a way to hold indirect exposure without the daily reset mechanics.

00:08:40.769 --> 00:08:45.509
The economic club of Canada hosts Governor Tiff Maclam on November 24th on the

00:08:45.509 --> 00:08:51.669
outlook and monetary policy challenges, according to the Bank of Canada, with remarks at 1025

00:08:51.669 --> 00:08:57.549
Eastern, an embargoed text at 1225, and a press conference around two in the afternoon.

00:08:58.149 --> 00:09:03.289
Rate-sensitive groups such as utilities and real estate investment trusts or REITs often

00:09:03.289 --> 00:09:08.449
reprise on shifts in forward guidance language, so reviewing those holdings ahead of the remarks

00:09:08.449 --> 00:09:09.789
