00:09:32.348 --> 00:09:41.357
Matched window alpha versus the NASDAQ, averaged per trade stands at plus 0.76% across 59 rules-based

00:09:41.357 --> 00:09:48.157
trades. 34 of those 59 trades beat the index over their own windows, while the total across all

00:09:48.157 --> 00:09:56.217
positions sits at minus $293.60, and with a T statistic of plus 0.99, the result remains

00:09:56.217 --> 00:10:03.157
early and not yet distinguishable from luck. The full history since March 2026 covers 110 trades

00:10:03.157 --> 00:10:11.297
with a 52 percent win rate and cumulative P&amp;L of minus $802.70. The rules-based era that began

00:10:11.297 --> 00:10:18.537
August 18th, 2026, keeps fixed five session holds, next open entries, and stop or horizon exits

00:10:18.537 --> 00:10:23.697
separate from earlier discretionary trades, and the process is now waiting sector rotation

00:10:23.697 --> 00:10:27.277
confirmation more heavily after names that skipped that filter.

00:10:28.243 --> 00:10:34.503
Contribution room in a TFSA does not grow when a holding falls from $10,000 to $6,000,

00:10:34.923 --> 00:10:37.483
and Motley Fool Canada walks through that arithmetic.

00:10:38.083 --> 00:10:41.563
The $4,000 mark-to-market hit does not give room back.

00:10:42.043 --> 00:10:47.083
The Canada Revenue Agency tallies withdrawals, and it ignores losses whether you have sold

00:10:47.083 --> 00:10:47.543
or not.

00:10:48.163 --> 00:10:52.903
Pulling out the remaining $6,000 creates $6,000 of new room the following calendar year,

00:10:52.903 --> 00:11:00.803
and the original 10,000 never reappears, selling the position and leaving the cash inside the account also fails to generate new room.

00:11:01.323 --> 00:11:04.423
The tax agency is not running a sympathy desk for your losers.

00:11:05.163 --> 00:11:13.263
Keep a running spreadsheet of every contribution and withdrawal date across every TFSA provider before you replace a sold position in the same year.

00:11:13.743 --> 00:11:18.643
Because the Canada revenue agency does not automatically refresh statements with unused room.

00:11:18.643 --> 00:11:23.203
room. The misconception is that selling a loser frees the full original contribution.

00:11:23.763 --> 00:11:28.683
The fix is to treat only actual withdrawals as future room and to reallocate inside the

00:11:28.683 --> 00:11:34.683
account without caching out when you can. The same piece uses the iShares Core S&amp;P TSX

00:11:34.683 --> 00:11:45.443
capped Composite Index ETF at $57.76 per unit. $6,000 buys 103 whole units for $5,949

00:11:45.443 --> 00:11:50.483
dollars and 28 cents before fees, with a small cash remainder left to deploy later.

00:11:51.083 --> 00:11:55.603
That leftover cash can wait inside the account for the next ad without creating a withdrawal

00:11:55.603 --> 00:11:56.903
you will then have to track.

00:11:57.887 --> 00:12:02.927
Your brokerage screener can run the defensive filter in under 10 minutes, set beta below

00:12:02.927 --> 00:12:10.047
0.8 and dividend coverage above 1.5 times, sort the TSX utilities list by payout ratio,

00:12:10.647 --> 00:12:13.267
and write down the top three names with their current yields.

